nder's Palace","shared_categories":"American (New), American (Traditional), Bars, Cajun/Creole, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":6},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"American (New), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"HJxqXDJFJsm3YVDYms0VCQ","review_id":"DPvqgX5hBOSuR9WqPjgmyA","date":"2015-07-23T18:11:47","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9360685348510742,"text_excerpt":"We hit this as our last stop eat while in New Orleans and we were not disappointed. I think we hit the restaurant at a good time. Slightly past lunch time on a Monday so the crowd was low and the staff was sober. We ordered a plethora of items to really taste the menu. We had the turtle soup which was like the most amazing chili we had ever had. The gumbo was decent and the stuffed crab was tasty. The crawfish étouffée was very flavorful (and I managed to mix in a little bit of turtle soup and that really kicked it up a notch!). Overall a very nice meal in a pleasant atmosphere. Just be warned- the bill is steep!"},{"business_id":"HJxqXDJFJsm3YVDYms0VCQ","review_id":"VXYB1TmafF_iyng7iSXUlw","date":"2011-02-05T04:58:09","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9289552569389343,"text_excerpt":"Ate here because it was close to the hotel where I was staying--the group I was with was hungry and were told this was a good place to go for something quick. The service was very friendly, and the food came very quickly. The prices are pretty reasonable, especially considering that so many places are incredibly overpriced and underwhelming in the French Quarter. In New Orleans, I am always a bit worried about the options for food, being a vegetarian (which is a term not generally heard of within Louisiana). Looking at the menu, there was one vegetarian pizza. Having just had really bad frozen pizza the day before that I needed to get out of my memory, this was the perfect option. I added..."},{"business_id":"HJxqXDJFJsm3YVDYms0VCQ","review_id":"TSg4ZbGOSFs_gKH3ZDlqNg","date":"2008-05-30T15:08:48","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9287740588188171,"text_excerpt":"I enjoyed my experience here, though I didn't have a full meal. We wandered in on our first day, and I promptly ordered an Abita Amber to fight off the heat. The extremely friendly bartender then convinced us not only to order a half dozen raw oysters, but also the sampler plate of all the baked ones they have. Both were excellent, the raw oysters being briny and extremely fresh. In fact, the oysters here were so good that my friend wouldn't get them anywhere else on the trip, as she was afraid it would ruin the experience for her."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"HJxqXDJFJsm3YVDYms0VCQ","photo_id":"pt3W5Hv1CXwcW7de5WhaXg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/pt3W5Hv1CXwcW7de5WhaXg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.